// Title: Service StartupType Change Via Sc.EXE
// ID: 85c312b7-f44d-4a51-a024-d671c40b49fc
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-01
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1685
// Description: Detect the use of "sc.exe" to change the startup type of a service to "disabled" or "demand"
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_ config *" and process.command_line like "*_start*") and (process.command_line like "*_disabled*" or process.command_line like "*_demand*")) and ((process.executable endswith "\\sc.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "sc.exe")))
